---
/* Where each of these Falco came from, and where each of them went.

   A thin wrapper over the kit's BranchRivers, which has drawn families of one
   surname as lanes since it was promoted out of Defranceschi. This file used
   to be 182 lines of SVG that copied that figure BY HAND — its old comment
   said so outright, «the same visual grammar as the de Franceschi archive's
   strands figure, which David asked this one to match» — and the five bands
   were a JavaScript array inside it. Both are gone: the drawing is the kit's
   and the bands are src/data/strands.json.

   WHY THIS ARCHIVE'S FIGURE IS THE OTHER WAY ROUND. The de Franceschi lanes
   are five families arriving in Istria from five directions. The Falco
   problem is the opposite shape: ONE line that stays put for seven
   generations and then crosses the world in a single lifetime, and FOUR other
   groups of the surname this archive can name and cannot join to it. So the
   first lane is the line and the rest are the strands it is not.

   THE FIVE HOUSEHOLDS ON STRADA CAMELLARA ARE DELIBERATELY NOT HERE. They
   never move, and a figure about where people came from would have to invent
   a journey for them. They are on /lines, in the band that exists to say
   «these do not connect».

   EVERY NODE IS A DOCUMENT. Nothing in this figure is inferred, and the
   numbers in the last lane are counts of harvested rows, not of people. */
import BranchRivers from "@daviddef/archive-kit/components/BranchRivers.astro";
import data from "../data/strands.json";
import line from "../data/line.json";

/* LANE STATUSES, PENS AND PERSON LINKS (kit 341af33, kit/docs/lines.md). Each lane says how far its own
   evidence reaches (status, span, statusNote in strands.json); the two pens say what is in them and why; the
   line's people are the generations of src/data/line.json (the gate allows a person in one place only, so the
   two a node links to are not repeated in the member list), named here from that file, so the list reads as
   names and not as slugs. The gate is `npm run check:lines`; the counts in the figure's heading are derived
   from this data by the kit and are never typed. */
const gens = new Map(line.map((g) => [g.gen, g.name]));
const SLUG_GEN = {
  "matteo-falco-of-matteo-falco-francesca-crisci": 1,
  "pasquale-falco-of-pasquale-falco-chiara-rivetti": 2,
  "vincenzo-falco-of-vincenzo-falco-andreana-crisci": 3,
  "raffaele-falco-of-raffaele-falco-angela-rosa-morgill": 4,
  "carmine-antonio-falco": 5,
  "raffaele-falco-2": 6,
  "carmine-antonio-falco-of-carmine-antonio-falco-filomena-ann": 7,
  "carmine-falco-of-carmine-antonio-falco-filomena-ann": 8,
};
const names = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(SLUG_GEN).map(([slug, g]) => [slug, `${gens.get(g)} (generation ${g})`]));
---
<BranchRivers rivers={data} caption={data.caption} title={data.title} personBase="/people/" names={names} />
